msub> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mtext>N</mtext><msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo><mtext>N</mtext><msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math>","difficulty":"Easy","source":"JEE Advanced 2017 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b16a60f23ac7d519f9b3da","_advSection":"SC","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect"},{"id":24867,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrogen","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Hydrogen peroxide in its reaction with KIO<sub>4</sub> and NH<sub>2</sub>OH respectively, is acting as a","options":["reducing agent, oxidising agent","reducing agent, reducing agent","oxidising agent, oxidising agent","oxidising agent, reducing agent"],"answer":0,"solution":"<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> In this reaction<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>  act as reducing agent<br  /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> In this reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> act as oxidising agent.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JEE Advanced 2014 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b16a3bf23ac7d519f9b28e","_advSection":"SC","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect"},{"id":24868,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrogen","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"The reagent(s) used for softening the temporary hardness of water is(are)","options":["$\\mathrm{Ca}_3\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_4\\right)_2$","$\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$","$\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3$","$\\mathrm{NaOCl}$"],"answer":1,"solution":"Softening the temporary hardness of water means conversion of bicarbonate into calcium carbonate (precipitation)\n\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\mathrm{Ca}\\left(\\mathrm{HCO}_3\\right)_2+\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2 \\longrightarrow \\\\\n2 \\mathrm{CaCO}_3 \\downarrow+2 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\\\\n\\mathrm{Ca}\\left(\\mathrm{HCO}_3\\right)_2+\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3 \\longrightarrow \\\\\n\\mathrm{CaCO}_3 \\downarrow+2 \\mathrm{NaHCO}_3\n\\end{gathered}\n\nEven $\\mathrm{NaOCl}$ can be used, as in aqueous medium $\\overline{\\mathrm{O}} \\mathrm{Cl}$ gets hydrolysed and makes solution alkaline enough to cause precipitation of $\\mathrm{CaCO}_3$.\n\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{NaOCl}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} & \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{HOCl}+\\mathrm{NaOH} \\\\\n\\mathrm{OH}^{-}+\\mathrm{HCO}_3^{-} & \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CO}_3^{2-}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\n\\end{aligned}\n\nRepresentative elements (Hydrogen and its compounds)\nConceptual\nII","difficulty":"Hard","source":"JEE Advanced 2010 (Paper 1)","_marksId":"64b169fef23ac7d519f9b05d","_advSection":"MC","questionType":"multipleCorrect","type":"multipleCorrect","answers":[1,2,3]}]}